# Lava Burst's damage to a creature can't be dealt instead to another permanent or player (its ruling; CR 614.9), so Jade
# Monolith's "the next time a source of your choice would deal damage to target creature this turn, that source deals that
# damage to you instead" does nothing to it. Bot2 casts Lava Burst with X 2 at Bot1's Phyrexian Walker (0/3); in response Bot1
# activates Jade Monolith targeting the Walker and chooses the Lava Burst on the stack as the source (CR 609.7a). The Walker
# is dealt the 2 damage and Bot1 none.

